course: dictionary
lesson: 2823
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. The easiest way to find the right one is to read the words around it. «Then he went in goal for the Year 3s' lunchtime match, dived full length in the mud and saved a penalty.» Goal, mud and saving a penalty tell you dived means threw his whole body quickly to the ground, not swimming.
explain: Dive has many meanings, so check the clues. Can you dive into a swimming pool? Yes. Can you dive into a bush? Yes, but that means moving quickly, not swimming. «At the eagle call they dive into bushes» shows the monkeys move fast to get out of danger.
explain: Some words are about rules and safety. Never dive into shallow water, or water you cannot see the bottom of. You can break your neck. Always check the depth and obey «No diving» signs.
fact: Dive means to jump into water head first, with your arms in front.
fact: Dive can also mean to swim under water, sometimes with special breathing equipment, like scuba divers on a coral reef.
fact: Dive can mean to move or drop quickly downwards, like a bird diving for fish, or to jump quickly to one side or to the ground, like a goalkeeper.
fact: «Diving» in football means pretending to be fouled to win a free kick. It is cheating and can earn a yellow card.
fact: Past tense: dived is British and dove is more common in America. «Americans often say dove where British say dived.»
exercise: «Then he went in goal and dived full length in the mud to save a penalty.» What does dived mean here? | Walked slowly off the pitch | *Jumped quickly to the ground to stop the ball | Fell asleep on the grass | Went swimming in a pool
exercise: «At the eagle call they dive into bushes.» What does dive mean here? | Sing loudly | Stand very still | Swim under the water in the bushes | *Move quickly into the bushes to get away
exercise: «Faking a fall in football to win a free kick is called diving.» What is diving in football? | Jumping into a swimming pool | *Pretending to be fouled to win a free kick | Scoring a goal from far away | Practising penalties alone
test: Which word means to jump into water head first with your arms in front? | Wade | *Dive | Float | Stroll
test: «Dive down and the light fades like evening.» What happens below about a thousand metres? | The light stays the same | The water turns red | *Sunlight is gone completely | The light gets brighter
exam: In British English, what is the past tense of dive? | *dived | diving | dove | dives
